# These files are consumed by Linux: a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for
# an interpreter literally named "bash\r", and systemd chokes on CRLF in a unit
# file. Pin them to LF so they survive a clone from any client, whatever that
# client's core.autocrlf happens to be set to.
*.sh              text eol=lf
*.service         text eol=lf
*.env.example     text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.docx binary
*.db   binary
